+### Tailnet access
+
+Set `tailscaleClientId` and at least one comma-separated `tailscaleTags` value
+to give new sandboxes Tailnet access without an auth-key secret. Configure the
+Tailscale workload identity provider for issuer `https://oidc.modal.com`,
+audience `oidc.modal.com`, and claims that constrain the intended Modal
+workspace, environment, and app. Its role must allow auth-key creation for the
+same tags. The plugin requests Modal's short-lived OIDC token, joins an
+explicitly preauthorized ephemeral node, and keeps Tailscale state in memory.
+
+Tailnet policy remains the authorization boundary. Grant the configured tag
+only the services, tagged devices, subnets, and ports that sandbox agents need.
+The standard image routes TCP from the BB daemon and its child agent processes
+through Tailscale's userspace network stack. It does not provide transparent
+UDP routing. Existing sandboxes must be replaced or resumed into fresh compute
+after enabling the settings because Modal decides whether to inject OIDC when
+it creates the sandbox.
+
